  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather will persist for most of the \nupcoming week. Below normal temperatures with frost and/or \nfreeze conditions are expected each night and early morning \nthrough the middle of the upcoming week.\n\nThe mid/upper trough will deamplify but linger across the \neastern U.S. through at least Tuesday with the axis shifting \ntoward the east as a well amplified ridge extends from the Gulf \nCoast across the OH Valley and into the Great Lakes region. \nMoisture will remain very limited given this pattern especially \nwith the surface high also helping to suppress any return flow \nthrough the upcoming week. This period of dry weather will add \nto the rainfall deficiencies the area has experienced so far \nthis year. ILM's departure from normal is more than 11 inches, \nFlorence and Lumberton more than 10 inches, and more than 20 \ninches in the Myrtle Beach area!\n\nIn addition to the dry conditions the swath of cold air \nsupported by high pressure over the MS valley will result in \nfreezing temperatures tonight into early Sunday morning. Coastal\nareas are expected to be slightly warmer, but will experience \nareas of frost, especially away from the beaches. As a result, \nplan to maintain the current Freeze Warning for inland areas, \nand introduce a Frost Advisory for the remaining coastal areas. \nFrost looks likely again Sunday night into early Monday morning,\nwith a few spots reaching freezing again. Frost is a good bet \nlate each night into the early morning, especially inland areas \nthrough the middle of the upcoming week.",
